{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "t13-eviction-running-never-cap-exceeded",
  "description": "T13 bilateral CLI observation (expected match), item 13 of the versioned inventory (contract decision 9/L9): with LOHRA_MAX_SUBSESSIONS=1, spawning a second child while the first is still running (gated, definitely in-flight — not terminal) leaves the registry at 2 entries, over cap, with neither evicted: eviction only ever removes a TERMINAL entry, and there is none to remove. Both children are later collected successfully by their own real sub_id, proving neither was silently dropped. Deterministic by construction: each child is released by its own dedicated gate, opened by a separate parent probe step, so there is no ambiguity about which child is still running when the second is spawned (both, the whole time, until explicitly released).",
  "argv": [
    "chat",
    "SCEN:parent spawn two running children over a cap of one",
    "--json",
    "--provider",
    "ollama",
    "--model",
    "stub-coder:1b"
  ],
  "environment": {
    "allow": ["LOHRA_MAX_SUBSESSIONS"],
    "set": {
      "PATH": "/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin",
      "PYTHONUTF8": "1",
      "PYTHONHASHSEED": "0",
      "NO_COLOR": "1",
      "LOHRA_NO_WIZARD": "1",
      "COLUMNS": "80",
      "TZ": "UTC",
      "HOME": "{{home}}",
      "LOHRA_HOME": "{{home}}/.lohra",
      "CODEX_HOME": "{{home}}/codex",
      "TMPDIR": "{{home}}/tmp",
      "LOHRA_MAX_SUBSESSIONS": "1"
    }
  },
  "preconditions": [
    {
      "kind": "tcp-port-closed",
